<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Marmara Ereğlisi</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Marmara Eregli</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Marmara Ereğlisi is a town on the northern shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-marmara">Sea of Marmara</a> in Tekirdağ Province, European <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>. It occupies the site of ancient Perinthus, a Samian colony that resisted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-ii-of-macedon">Philip II of Macedon</a> in 340 BCE and later, renamed Heraclea, became the capital of the Roman province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a>. Remains of the ancient city survive around the modern town.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/marmara-ereglisi.jpg" alt="Marmara Ereğlisi" width="320" height="208" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CeeGee · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:MarmaraEre%C4%9Flisi_(1).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
